From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:05:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ofono_push_notification: clean values, a quota, a broken
 message alone

A notification is an SMS anyone can send, and what the fetched message
says ends up in files mmsd reads again at its next start:

- The Transaction-Id or Message-ID of the fetched message went into the
  .status file as it was, line breaks included: 'T1\nstate=sent' added a
  line of its own, and the message came back as a sent one. Every value
  of the .status and .headers files is now one line without control
  characters.
- A SMIL part with invalid UTF-8 raised after the files were written and
  the MMSC was told the message arrived, so it was lost; at each start
  the export of the old messages broke off at it, and none after it were
  shown. The text is decoded with replacement now, and each old message
  is exported on its own.
- Each notification with a new Content-Location could bring up to 5 MiB:
  no new fetch once the stored messages take 50 MiB, and at most 8
  fetches open at once.

- A fetched message that cannot be stored or decoded is marked
  download_failed instead of staying announced as downloading.
